# Wireshark Network Traffic Analysis Lab

## 📌 Overview
This lab demonstrates hands-on experience with network traffic analysis using Wireshark.
The work is based on practical exercises from TryHackMe and focuses on HTTP traffic,
packet inspection, metadata analysis, and expert information.

## 🧰 Tools Used
- Wireshark
- Linux (Ubuntu)
- TCP/IP, HTTP
- md5sum

## 🔍 Lab Tasks

### 1. HTTP Traffic Analysis
- Identified HTTP GET requests
- Inspected headers and payload
- Verified content type and server response



---

### 2. Follow TCP Stream
- Reconstructed full HTTP conversation
- Extracted HTML content
- Located embedded parameters



---

### 3. Packet Comments
- Located packet comments in frame 12
- Extracted embedded message
- Calculated MD5 hash of the comment string


---

### 4. String Search in Packets
- Searched for specific strings (e.g. `r4w`)
- Identified application-layer content
- Extracted relevant fields from HTTP responses



---

### 5. Expert Information
- Reviewed malformed packets and warnings
- Analyzed protocol-level issues
- Counted warnings and errors



---

## ✅ Key Skills Demonstrated
- Network traffic inspection
- HTTP protocol analysis
- Packet filtering and searching
- TCP stream reconstruction
- Security-focused traffic investigation

## 🚀 Notes
This lab represents practical SOC-style analysis and entry-level blue team skills.
